Article 20

1. Social Protection as referred to in Article 19 paragraph (2) letter a is in the form of support to ensure the survival of Women from social vulnerability in order to ensure the fulfillment of a decent standard of living.
2. Medical protection as referred to in Article 19 paragraph (2) letter b is in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of the victim carried out by medical personnel and paramedics at the nearest health service facility from the victim in accordance with the victim's needs.
3. Legal protection as referred to in Article 19 paragraph (2) letter c is in the form of Services and Assistance to help victims go through the legal and judicial process by providing legal aid, legal consultation and legal Assistance to victims.
4. Economic protection as referred to in Article 19 paragraph (2) letter d is in the form of services for skills and to provide economic access in accordance with the identification of economic empowerment needs of the victim by taking into account:
a. age;
b. level of education;
c. expertise;
d. interests and talents;
e. experience in participating in training; and/ or
f. work history.
5. Psychological Protection as referred to in Article 19 paragraph (2) letter e is in the form of psychological support so that victims have self-confidence, are capable of being independent in solving problems.
